IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cta-community`

-- Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) -- the Q&A layer: the questions people ask, with the seat and the situation as
-- parameters.
--
-- PURPOSE. One module whose exported questions serve every seat from one deployment. Every exported question takes
-- `my role` first ("Which of these describes you"). A question about another role answers `does not arise for you`
-- without reading any other input, so the site's question form never asks those inputs and drops the question.
--
-- ROLES. The baseline (cta-community.l4) was written from the seat of the lot owner, and, before settlement, the buyer
-- about to become one. Here they are two roles, and two more are added:
--   - the owner of a lot: the community corporation, contributions, votes, by-laws, own duties, certificates, disputes;
--   - the buyer of a lot (before or at settlement): ss 130-138, and the s 97 certificate a buyer may ask for (s 94(2)(c));
--   - the seller of a lot: what ss 130, 131, 137 and 138 require of the seller;
--   - an occupier or lessee who does not own the lot: the by-laws apply to them (s 44(1)(d)-(e), (3)), and so do ss 70
--     and 71 and the Tribunal's enforcement (s 48).
-- The community corporation, its council, the Tribunal, the Registrar and the Planning Commission are never seats.
-- What the corporation may or must do (levy, charge interest, spend, enforce, certify) appears as what it means for the
-- person asking.
--
-- SITUATIONS (design D8 of the Graffiti Vandalism Act encoding). Within a role, a question that arises only in a
-- situation takes that situation's fact straight after `my role`, and answers `does not arise for you` when it does not
-- hold, without reading anything else. The questions of one situation share one input (same name, type and @desc).
--   - `my lot's tier` (`Tier`): the s 88(3) question of a tier 1 levy reaching a tier 2 owner arises only for a tier 2
--     lot. Not `tier 2`: does not arise. (The s 17 and s 16(7) questions also take it, second, as an ordinary input.)
--   - `the community corporation has served me a notice of a contribution` (BOOLEAN): s 88(4)-(5). FALSE: does not arise.
--   - `a contribution of mine was not paid by its due date` (BOOLEAN): s 88(1)(f)-(g) interest. FALSE: does not arise.
--   - `I bought my lot from a previous owner` (BOOLEAN): ss 88(6), 97(3). FALSE: does not arise.
--   - `my contributions are overdue` (BOOLEAN, the baseline's input): s 106(13)(c), (14)(b), whether I can vote even so.
--     FALSE: does not arise. ("Who may cast my lot's vote" also takes it, as an ordinary input.)
--   - `I have been given a notice that I broke a by-law` (BOOLEAN): s 48(2), for the owner and the occupier.
--   - `someone else has broken a scheme by-law` (BOOLEAN): s 48(3)-(4), for the owner and the occupier.
--   - `the Tribunal has made an order in my community titles dispute` (BOOLEAN): s 175. FALSE: does not arise.
--   - `something changed after the contract was signed and before settlement` (BOOLEAN): s 3(1), ss 131, 134-136, for the
--     buyer and the seller. FALSE: does not arise.
--   - `the contract is for a lot not yet created (off the plan)` (BOOLEAN): s 137, for the buyer and the seller.
--   - `the contract to buy the lot has been avoided` (BOOLEAN): s 138(2), for the buyer and the seller.
-- A question that arises in every situation of its role takes no situation input.
--
-- The rules are in cta-community.l4. This module calls them and restates none; for the owner and the buyer each answer
-- is the baseline export's own answer, wrapped. The seller's and occupier's questions use the baseline's rules where
-- they exist, and small helpers below where they do not. No exported question takes a DEONTIC or EVENT input.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md, "Q&A layer (seat and situations as parameters)".

§ `Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I own a lot in a community titles scheme`
    `I am buying a lot in a community titles scheme`
    `I am selling a lot in a community titles scheme`
    `I occupy or lease a lot in a community titles scheme, but do not own it`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

-- A relative unit entitlement is a lot's unit entitlement over "the sum of the unit entitlements of all the lots and
-- tier parcels in the community titles scheme" (s 3(1)); s 41(1)(a) gives each lot and tier parcel "a whole number (a
-- unit entitlement)", so a scheme's sum is never 0. The baseline divides by the sums given; where a sum given is 0 (not
-- a real scheme), the layer answers that no value can be worked out instead of dividing by 0.
DECLARE `Amount` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `no amount can be worked out: a sum of unit entitlements given is 0, and every scheme's sum is above 0 (ss 3(1), 41(1)(a))`
    amount HAS dollars IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Share` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `no share can be worked out: a sum of unit entitlements given is 0, and every scheme's sum is above 0 (ss 3(1), 41(1)(a))`
    `a share of` HAS `the fraction` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Days` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `within` HAS `days` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `How I take part, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `How I take part`

DECLARE `Who casts my lot's vote, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `Who casts my lot's vote`

DECLARE `Notifiable variation, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `no answer can be worked out: a sum of unit entitlements given is 0, and every scheme's sum is above 0 (ss 3(1), 41(1)(a))`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `Notifiable variation`

-- s 131(3), (4)-(5): when the seller must tell the buyer of a notifiable variation, or of the completion of one the
-- contract described.
DECLARE `When I must tell the buyer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `notice of the variation, as soon as practicable`
    `notice of the variation, within 10 working days after I became aware of it`
    `notice of its completion only, as soon as practicable`
    `notice of its completion only, within 10 working days after I became aware of the completion`

§§ `Helpers`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

-- The sums of unit entitlements s 16(7) divides by, for my lot's tier: my scheme's (every tier), the scheme above's
-- (tiers 2 and 3) and the tier 1 scheme's (tier 3). Every value of `Tier` is listed (graffiti finding 31).
GIVEN `my lot's tier` IS A `Tier`
      `the sum in my scheme` IS A NUMBER
      `the sum in the scheme above` IS A NUMBER
      `the sum in the tier 1 scheme` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a s 16(7) sum is 0 for` `my lot's tier` `the sum in my scheme` `the sum in the scheme above` `the sum in the tier 1 scheme` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my lot's tier`
    WHEN `tier 1` THEN `the sum in my scheme` AT MOST 0
    WHEN `tier 2` THEN `the sum in my scheme` AT MOST 0 OR `the sum in the scheme above` AT MOST 0
    WHEN `tier 3` THEN `the sum in my scheme` AT MOST 0 OR `the sum in the scheme above` AT MOST 0 OR `the sum in the tier 1 scheme` AT MOST 0

-- s 131(3), (5): "(a) if the seller becomes aware ... less than 15 working days before the settlement date ... as soon as
-- practicable; and (b) in any other case -- not later than 10 working days after the seller becomes aware". s 131(4):
-- no notice of the variation is needed if the contract described it and it was completed as described; notice of the
-- completion is then due in the same times (s 131(4)(c), (5)). The encoder reads "the contract described it and it
-- matched" as (4)(a)-(b); (4)(c) is the notice this answer then names.
GIVEN `the contract described it and it was completed as described` IS A BOOLEAN
      `working days before settlement when I became aware` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `When I must tell the buyer`
`the s 131 time for` `the contract described it and it was completed as described` `working days before settlement when I became aware` MEANS
    IF `the contract described it and it was completed as described`
    THEN IF `working days before settlement when I became aware` LESS THAN 15
         THEN `notice of its completion only, as soon as practicable`
         ELSE `notice of its completion only, within 10 working days after I became aware of the completion`
    ELSE IF `working days before settlement when I became aware` LESS THAN 15
         THEN `notice of the variation, as soon as practicable`
         ELSE `notice of the variation, within 10 working days after I became aware of it`

-- s 3(1), reg 8: the relative unit entitlement before and after divides by the notified sum and the sum now.
GIVEN `the change` IS A `What changed before settlement`
GIVETH A `Notifiable variation, if it arises`
`the variation kind, unless a sum is 0` `the change` MEANS
    IF `the change`'s `the notified sum of unit entitlements` AT MOST 0 OR `the change`'s `the sum of unit entitlements now` AT MOST 0
    THEN `no answer can be worked out: a sum of unit entitlements given is 0, and every scheme's sum is above 0 (ss 3(1), 41(1)(a))`
    ELSE `the answer is` (`What kind of notifiable variation is it` `the change`)

§§ `For the owner of a lot`

§§§ `ss 16, 17 -- the community corporation and my place in it`

@export How do I, as a lot owner, take part in this community corporation: as a member myself, through my own community corporation, or not at all (Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) s 17(6)-(8))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my lot's tier` IS A `Tier` @desc The tier of the community titles scheme your lot is in
      `the corporation's tier` IS A `Tier` @desc The tier of the community titles scheme whose corporation you are asking about
      `my scheme is that scheme or belongs to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your lot's scheme is that scheme, or a scheme that belongs to it (a tier 2 or tier 3 scheme carved out of it)
GIVETH A `How I take part, if it arises`
`How do I as a lot owner take part in this community corporation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN `the answer is` (`How do I take part in this community corporation` `my lot's tier` `the corporation's tier` `my scheme is that scheme or belongs to it`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is my undivided share in the tier 1 common property of the whole community scheme, as a fraction (Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) s 16(7))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my lot's tier` IS A `Tier` @desc The tier of the community titles scheme your lot is in
      `my lot's unit entitlement` IS A NUMBER @desc Your lot's unit entitlement, from your scheme's schedule of unit entitlements
      `the sum in my scheme` IS A NUMBER @desc The sum of the unit entitlements of all lots and tier parcels in your scheme
      `my scheme's parcel unit entitlement` IS A NUMBER @desc For a tier 2 or tier 3 lot: the unit entitlement of your scheme's tier parcel in the scheme above it (0 for a tier 1 lot)
      `the sum in the scheme above` IS A NUMBER @desc The sum of the unit entitlements in the scheme above yours (1 for a tier 1 lot)
      `the tier 2 parcel's unit entitlement in tier 1` IS A NUMBER @desc For a tier 3 lot: the unit entitlement of the tier 2 scheme's parcel in the tier 1 scheme (0 otherwise)
      `the sum in the tier 1 scheme` IS A NUMBER @desc For a tier 3 lot: the sum of the unit entitlements in the tier 1 scheme (1 otherwise)
GIVETH A `Share`
`What is my undivided share in the tier 1 common property` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN
        IF `a s 16(7) sum is 0 for` `my lot's tier` `the sum in my scheme` `the sum in the scheme above` `the sum in the tier 1 scheme`
        THEN `no share can be worked out: a sum of unit entitlements given is 0, and every scheme's sum is above 0 (ss 3(1), 41(1)(a))`
        ELSE `a share of` (`What is my share of the tier 1 common property` `my lot's tier` `my lot's unit entitlement` `the sum in my scheme` `my scheme's parcel unit entitlement` `the sum in the scheme above` `the tier 2 parcel's unit entitlement in tier 1` `the sum in the tier 1 scheme`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 85, 87, 88 -- contributions, the funds and interest`

@export How much must I pay as my lot's share of a contribution my community corporation has resolved to raise, in dollars (Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) s 88(2), (3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the amount resolved` IS A NUMBER @desc The total, in dollars, the community corporation resolved to raise from its members (or, under s 88(3), the amount levied on your corporation by the corporation above it)
      `my unit entitlement` IS A NUMBER @desc The unit entitlement of your lot (or of your scheme's tier parcel, when working out what the corporation above levies on your corporation)
      `the sum of the unit entitlements` IS A NUMBER @desc The sum of the unit entitlements of all lots and tier parcels in the scheme
      `the by-laws provide a different method` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the scheme by-laws provide a different method of apportionment for this contribution
      `my share under the by-law method` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, your share under it, as a fraction (for example 0.05); otherwise 0
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much is my share of the contribution` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN
        IF (NOT `the by-laws provide a different method`) AND (`the sum of the unit entitlements` AT MOST 0)
        THEN `no amount can be worked out: a sum of unit entitlements given is 0, and every scheme's sum is above 0 (ss 3(1), 41(1)(a))`
        ELSE amount (`How much is my contribution` `the amount resolved` `my unit entitlement` `the sum of the unit entitlements` `the by-laws provide a different method` `my share under the by-law method`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How much of a levy raised by the tier 1 community corporation reaches me, a tier 2 lot owner, through my own corporation, in dollars (Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) s 88(2), (3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my lot's tier` IS A `Tier` @desc The tier of the community titles scheme your lot is in
      `the tier 1 levy` IS A NUMBER @desc The total, in dollars, the tier 1 corporation resolved to raise from its members
      `my tier 2 parcel's unit entitlement` IS A NUMBER @desc The unit entitlement of your tier 2 scheme's parcel in the tier 1 schedule
      `the sum of the tier 1 unit entitlements` IS A NUMBER @desc The sum of the unit entitlements of all lots and tier parcels in the tier 1 scheme
      `my lot's unit entitlement` IS A NUMBER @desc Your lot's unit entitlement, from your scheme's schedule of unit entitlements
      `the sum in my scheme` IS A NUMBER @desc The sum of the unit entitlements of all lots and tier parcels in your scheme
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much of the tier 1 levy reaches me as a tier 2 owner` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN
        IF `my lot's tier` EQUALS `tier 2`
        THEN IF `the sum of the tier 1 unit entitlements` AT MOST 0 OR `the sum in my scheme` AT MOST 0
             THEN `no amount can be worked out: a sum of unit entitlements given is 0, and every scheme's sum is above 0 (ss 3(1), 41(1)(a))`
             ELSE amount (`How much of the tier 1 levy reaches me` `the tier 1 levy` `my tier 2 parcel's unit entitlement` `the sum of the tier 1 unit entitlements` `my lot's unit entitlement` `the sum in my scheme`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must my community corporation keep a reserve fund and a 10 year plan, so that I will be levied for it (Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) s 85(1), (2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must my community corporation keep a reserve fund and a 10 year plan` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN `yes if` `Must my community corporation keep a reserve fund`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is the contribution notice my community corporation served on me a valid one, so that the contribution falls due on its date (Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) s 88(4), (5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the community corporation has served me a notice of a contribution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the community corporation has served on you a notice of a contribution or instalment it wants you to pay
      `it states the amount, the due date and the split between the funds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice states the amount, the date for payment and how it is split between the administrative and reserve funds
      `it states any arrears and what paying late will cost` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it states any amount already outstanding and the amount or interest rate that applies if you pay late
      `days between service and the due date` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days before the date for payment the notice was served on you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is the contribution notice served on me valid` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN
        IF `the community corporation has served me a notice of a contribution`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is my contribution notice valid` `it states the amount, the due date and the split between the funds` `it states any arrears and what paying late will cost` `days between service and the due date`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How much interest can my community corporation charge me on a contribution I paid late, or have not paid, in dollars (Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) s 88(1)(e)-(g); reg 79)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `a contribution of mine was not paid by its due date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a contribution or instalment of yours to the community corporation was not paid by its due date (paid late, or still unpaid)
      `the amount unpaid` IS A NUMBER @desc The contribution or instalment, in dollars, left unpaid after it fell due
      `the days it was overdue` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days from the due date until it was paid
      `the contribution was inflated for an early-payment discount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the corporation used the inflate-and-discount method for this contribution instead of interest
      `my corporation fixed an arrears interest rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the corporation has fixed, by ordinary resolution, a rate of interest on arrears
      `the rate it fixed` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, that yearly rate as a fraction (for example 0.1 for 10%); otherwise 0
      `it set a lesser rate or none for my case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the corporation decided not to charge interest, or to charge less, in your case or a class of cases including yours
      `that lesser rate` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, that yearly rate as a fraction (0 for no interest); otherwise 0
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much interest can I be charged on a late contribution` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN
        IF `a contribution of mine was not paid by its due date`
        THEN amount (`How much interest do I owe` `the amount unpaid` `the days it was overdue` `the contribution was inflated for an early-payment discount` `my corporation fixed an arrears interest rate` `the rate it fixed` `it set a lesser rate or none for my case` `that lesser rate`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Having bought my lot, how much of the previous owner's unpaid contributions and interest can the community corporation make me pay, in dollars (Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) s 88(6), s 97(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I bought my lot from a previous owner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you became the owner of your lot by buying it from someone who owned it before you
      `the arrears at the certificate date` IS A NUMBER @desc Contributions and interest, in dollars, actually unpaid at the date of the s 97 certificate (or at settlement, if you had no certificate)
      `the arrears arising after the certificate date` IS A NUMBER @desc Contributions and interest, in dollars, that fell unpaid after the certificate date and before you became owner (0 if no certificate)
      `I bought with a s 97 certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you (or your settlement agent) obtained a certificate under s 97(2) for the lot before buying it
      `the arrears the certificate stated` IS A NUMBER @desc The outstanding amount the certificate stated, in dollars (0 if none)
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much of the previous owner's arrears can I be made to pay` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN
        IF `I bought my lot from a previous owner`
        THEN amount (`How much of the previous owner's arrears must I pay` `the arrears at the certificate date` `the arrears arising after the certificate date` `I bought with a s 97 certificate` `the arrears the certificate stated`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must a budget that spends on improving or altering the common property be approved by special resolution, so that my vote counts against it (Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) s 87(5); reg 77)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the improvement spending` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars the budget or variation provides for improving or altering the common property (not sustainability infrastructure)
      `the number of lots and tier parcels` IS A NUMBER @desc How many lots and tier parcels there are in the community titles scheme
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must this improvement budget pass by special resolution` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN `yes if` (`Must the improvement budget pass by special resolution` `the improvement spending` `the number of lots and tier parcels`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can my community corporation spend money that the approved budget does not authorise, without a further vote (Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) s 87(6); reg 78)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the unbudgeted spending this financial year` IS A NUMBER @desc Total dollars spent this financial year outside the approved budget, including the proposed item
      `the number of lots and tier parcels` IS A NUMBER @desc How many lots and tier parcels there are in the community titles scheme
      `a per-lot amount was fixed by special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the corporation has fixed its own amount per lot or tier parcel by special resolution
      `the per-lot amount fixed` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, that amount in dollars; otherwise 0
      `a court, tribunal or written-law notice requires it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court, the Tribunal or a notice or order under a written law requires the spending
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can my community corporation spend outside the approved budget` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN `yes if` (`Can the community corporation spend outside the budget` `the unbudgeted spending this financial year` `the number of lots and tier parcels` `a per-lot amount was fixed by special resolution` `the per-lot amount fixed` `a court, tribunal or written-law notice requires it`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 106, 107 -- my lot's vote`

@export Did the resolution pass as an ordinary resolution of my community corporation (Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) s 106(5), (6))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the unit entitlement voting for` IS A NUMBER @desc The total unit entitlement of the lots and tier parcels whose votes were cast in favour
      `the unit entitlement voting against` IS A NUMBER @desc The total unit entitlement of those whose votes were cast against
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Did the resolution pass as an ordinary resolution` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN `yes if` (`Did it pass as an ordinary resolution` `the unit entitlement voting for` `the unit entitlement voting against`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Did the resolution pass as a special resolution, the kind needed to make a by-law that binds me (Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) s 106(3), (7))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `14 days' notice of its terms was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every member got written notice of the terms and voting system at least 14 days before the vote
      `the number of members` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members the community corporation has (lot owners and member corporations)
      `the sum of the unit entitlements` IS A NUMBER @desc The sum of the unit entitlements of all lots and tier parcels in the scheme
      `the unit entitlement voting for` IS A NUMBER @desc The total unit entitlement of the lots and tier parcels whose votes were cast in favour
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Did the resolution pass as a special resolution` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN `yes if` (`Did it pass as a special resolution` `14 days' notice of its terms was given` `the number of members` `the sum of the unit entitlements` `the unit entitlement voting for`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can I cast my lot's vote on this resolution even though my contributions are overdue (Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) s 106(13)(c), (14)(b))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my contributions are overdue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any contribution of yours to the community corporation is overdue
      `the resolution` IS A `Kind of resolution` @desc The kind of resolution being voted on
      `the by-laws exclude members in arrears` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the scheme by-laws exclude members with overdue contributions from voting on ordinary resolutions
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I vote on this resolution although my contributions are overdue` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN
        IF `my contributions are overdue`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can I cast my lot's vote` `the resolution` `my contributions are overdue` `the by-laws exclude members in arrears`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Who may cast my lot's vote on a resolution of the community corporation (Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) ss 106(8), (13)(c), 107(5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the resolution` IS A `Kind of resolution` @desc The kind of resolution being voted on
      `my contributions are overdue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any contribution of yours to the community corporation is overdue
      `the by-laws exclude members in arrears` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the scheme by-laws exclude members with overdue contributions from voting on ordinary resolutions
      `I own the lot with co-owners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you own the lot together with someone else
      `I am present at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are present at the meeting where the vote is taken
GIVETH A `Who casts my lot's vote, if it arises`
`Who may cast the vote of my lot` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN `the answer is` (`Who may cast my lot's vote` `the resolution` `my contributions are overdue` `the by-laws exclude members in arrears` `I own the lot with co-owners` `I am present at the meeting`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 43-48 -- what the by-laws can and cannot do to me`

@export Is this by-law of my community titles scheme invalid against me (Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) s 47)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the by-law` IS A `What the by-law does` @desc What the by-law does, as a set of yes/no facts (the last one is the Tribunal's judgment)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is this by-law of my scheme invalid` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN `yes if` (`Is this by-law invalid` `the by-law`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Does this by-law bind me as an owner: was it made the way the Act requires, and is it valid (Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) ss 43(1)-(2), 44(2), 46(5), 47)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `it was registered with the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the by-law was among the scheme by-laws registered when the scheme was registered
      `it passed as a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the resolution that made it passed as a special resolution
      `it is an exclusive use by-law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it gives the occupiers of particular lots exclusive use of, or special privileges over, common property
      `every special lot owner consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether the owner of each such lot gave written consent
      `the by-law` IS A `What the by-law does` @desc What the by-law does, as a set of yes/no facts (the last one is the Tribunal's judgment)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does this by-law bind me as an owner` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN `yes if` (`Does this by-law bind me` `it was registered with the scheme` `it passed as a special resolution` `it is an exclusive use by-law` `every special lot owner consented in writing` `the by-law`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 72 -- my own duties as owner`

@export Must I nominate an agent in Australia to the community corporation (Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) s 72(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am ordinarily resident overseas` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you ordinarily live outside Australia
      `I am a body corporate not registered in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the owner is a company not registered in Australia
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I nominate an agent in Australia to the corporation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN `yes if` (`Must I nominate an agent in Australia` `I am ordinarily resident overseas` `I am a body corporate not registered in Australia`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 162, 175 -- challenging a decision`

@export Can I, as a lot owner, apply to the State Administrative Tribunal to resolve this dispute as a scheme dispute (Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) s 162)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the dispute` IS A `My dispute` @desc What the dispute is about
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I take this dispute to the Tribunal as a lot owner` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN `yes if` (`Can I take this dispute to the Tribunal` `the dispute`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can I apply for internal review of a Tribunal order made in my community titles dispute (Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) s 175; reg 173)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the Tribunal has made an order in my community titles dispute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the State Administrative Tribunal has made an order in a scheme dispute you are a party to
      `the order was made by a member who is not legally qualified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal member who made the order is not a legally qualified member
      `the Tribunal gives leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal gives leave for the internal review
      `days since the order` IS A NUMBER @desc Days since the order was made
      `the President extended the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the President has extended the 28-day period (and you are within it)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I seek internal review of the Tribunal's order` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN
        IF `the Tribunal has made an order in my community titles dispute`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can I seek internal review` `the order was made by a member who is not legally qualified` `the Tribunal gives leave` `days since the order` `the President extended the time`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the owner, and for an occupier or lessee who does not own the lot`

§§§ `ss 44, 48 -- the by-laws and their enforcement`

-- s 44(1)(d)-(e): by-laws may apply to "an occupier or lessee, for the time being, of a lot"; (2): each person to whom
-- they apply "must comply with the bylaws as if the bylaws were a deed"; (3): a lease of a lot "is taken to contain an
-- agreement by the lessee that the lessee will comply with the scheme bylaws". The owner's own question is "Does this
-- by-law bind me as an owner" above.
@export As an occupier or lessee, must I comply with the scheme by-laws (Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) s 44(1)(d), (2), (3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`As an occupier must I comply with the scheme by-laws` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I occupy or lease a lot in a community titles scheme, but do not own it` THEN yes
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 44(4): "The owner, occupier or lessee of a lot ... must take all steps that are reasonable in the circumstances to
-- ensure that every person who they permit to use or who they invite on to the lot or common property complies with
-- bylaws that apply to the owner, occupier or lessee."
@export Must I take reasonable steps to make sure the people I let use the lot, or invite on to it, keep the by-laws (Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) s 44(4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I see that my visitors keep the by-laws` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN yes
    WHEN `I occupy or lease a lot in a community titles scheme, but do not own it` THEN yes
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is the by-law breach notice my community corporation gave me a valid notice (Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) s 48(2); reg 59)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been given a notice that I broke a by-law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the community corporation has given you a written notice saying you broke a scheme by-law
      `it names the by-law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice specifies the particular by-law said to be broken
      `it states the facts relied on` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it specifies the facts relied on as evidence
      `it states what I must do or stop doing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it specifies what you must do or refrain from doing
      `it carries the regulations' explanation of s 48` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it includes the explanation of s 48 in the form of Schedule 1 to the regulations
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is the by-law breach notice given to me valid` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN
        IF `I have been given a notice that I broke a by-law`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is the breach notice valid` `it names the by-law` `it states the facts relied on` `it states what I must do or stop doing` `it carries the regulations' explanation of s 48`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    WHEN `I occupy or lease a lot in a community titles scheme, but do not own it` THEN
        IF `I have been given a notice that I broke a by-law`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is the breach notice valid` `it names the by-law` `it states the facts relied on` `it states what I must do or stop doing` `it carries the regulations' explanation of s 48`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 48(1)(b), (3), (4): the corporation, or a member, mortgagee or occupier, may apply on the same three grounds.
@export Can the community corporation (or another owner or occupier) take me to the Tribunal to enforce a by-law against me (Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) s 48(1)(b), (3), (4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `it seriously harmed someone else` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the breach had serious adverse consequences for someone other than you
      `the times I have broken that by-law` IS A NUMBER @desc On how many separate occasions you have broken that particular by-law
      `I broke a valid breach notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were given a written breach notice under s 48(1)(a) and then contravened it
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I be taken to the Tribunal to enforce a by-law against me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN `yes if` (`Can I be taken to the Tribunal over a by-law` `it seriously harmed someone else` `the times I have broken that by-law` `I broke a valid breach notice`)
    WHEN `I occupy or lease a lot in a community titles scheme, but do not own it` THEN `yes if` (`Can I be taken to the Tribunal over a by-law` `it seriously harmed someone else` `the times I have broken that by-law` `I broke a valid breach notice`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 48(3): "(a) a member of the community corporation" (the owner) and "(c) an occupier of a lot" may apply; (4): only on
-- the grounds that the person "has been given notice under subsection (1)(a) and has contravened the notice", that the
-- contravention "has had serious adverse consequences for a person other than the person alleged to have contravened",
-- or that the person "has contravened the particular scheme bylaw on at least 3 separate occasions" -- the grounds of
-- s 48(1)(b), so the baseline's rule for them is used with the other person's facts. (4)(a)'s "if a person other than
-- the community corporation is alleged to have contravened" is read as met: the question is about someone else, not the
-- corporation, breaking a by-law (the corporation's own breach is not covered).
@export May I apply to the Tribunal to enforce a by-law against someone else who broke it (Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) s 48(3), (4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `someone else has broken a scheme by-law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another owner, occupier or person on the scheme (not the community corporation) has broken a scheme by-law
      `it seriously harmed someone other than them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether their breach had serious adverse consequences for someone other than them
      `the times they have broken that by-law` IS A NUMBER @desc On how many separate occasions they have broken that particular by-law
      `they broke a breach notice the corporation gave them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the community corporation gave them a written breach notice under s 48(1)(a) and they then contravened it
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I apply to the Tribunal to enforce a by-law against someone else` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN
        IF `someone else has broken a scheme by-law`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can I be taken to the Tribunal over a by-law` `it seriously harmed someone other than them` `the times they have broken that by-law` `they broke a breach notice the corporation gave them`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    WHEN `I occupy or lease a lot in a community titles scheme, but do not own it` THEN
        IF `someone else has broken a scheme by-law`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can I be taken to the Tribunal over a by-law` `it seriously harmed someone other than them` `the times they have broken that by-law` `they broke a breach notice the corporation gave them`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most the Tribunal can order me to pay as a penalty for breaking a by-law, in dollars (Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) s 48(6)(c); reg 60)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most the Tribunal can make me pay for breaking a by-law` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN amount `What is the most I can be made to pay for a by-law breach`
    WHEN `I occupy or lease a lot in a community titles scheme, but do not own it` THEN amount `What is the most I can be made to pay for a by-law breach`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can the Tribunal impose a daily penalty on me for a continuing by-law breach (Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) s 48(6)(d))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can the Tribunal give me a daily penalty for a continuing by-law breach` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN `yes if` `Can I be given a daily penalty for a by-law breach`
    WHEN `I occupy or lease a lot in a community titles scheme, but do not own it` THEN `yes if` `Can I be given a daily penalty for a by-law breach`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 70, 71 -- the duties of an owner or occupier`

-- s 70 and s 71 both bind "an owner or occupier of a lot", so the baseline's rules serve the occupier unchanged.
@export What is the most I can be fined for using part of the scheme against a restricted use condition on the scheme plan, in dollars (Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) s 70)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the days or part days it continued` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days or part days the offence continued (0 for a single occasion)
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I can be fined for using the scheme against a restricted use condition` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN amount (`What is the most I can be fined for breaching a restricted use condition` `the days or part days it continued`)
    WHEN `I occupy or lease a lot in a community titles scheme, but do not own it` THEN amount (`What is the most I can be fined for breaching a restricted use condition` `the days or part days it continued`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I in breach of my duty not to interfere unreasonably with others' use and enjoyment (Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) s 71)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my use interferes with another lot or the common property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the way you use (or let others use) the lot or common property interferes with someone lawfully on another lot or the common property
      `the Tribunal would find it unreasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the interference is unreasonable, as the Tribunal would find
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I in breach of the use and enjoyment duty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN `yes if` (`Am I breaching the use and enjoyment duty` `my use interferes with another lot or the common property` `the Tribunal would find it unreasonable`)
    WHEN `I occupy or lease a lot in a community titles scheme, but do not own it` THEN `yes if` (`Am I breaching the use and enjoyment duty` `my use interferes with another lot or the common property` `the Tribunal would find it unreasonable`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the owner, and for the buyer of a lot`

§§§ `ss 94, 97 -- the certificate of what is owing`

-- s 94(2): a person with a proper interest includes "(a) a member of the community corporation" and "(c) a buyer who has
-- entered into a contract for the sale and purchase of a lot", so the certificate questions are asked of both.
@export What is the most my community corporation may charge me for a s 97 certificate, in dollars (Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) s 94(4); reg 84)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the corporation must remit GST for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the community corporation is required to remit GST on the fee
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I can be charged for a s 97 certificate` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN amount (`What is the most I can be charged for a certificate` `the corporation must remit GST for it`)
    WHEN `I am buying a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN amount (`What is the most I can be charged for a certificate` `the corporation must remit GST for it`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Within how many days must the community corporation give me the s 97 certificate after my application is duly made (Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) s 97(2); reg 84(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Days`
`Within how many days must I be given the s 97 certificate` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN `within` `Within how many days must I get the certificate`
    WHEN `I am buying a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN `within` `Within how many days must I get the certificate`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the buyer of a lot`

§§§ `ss 130, 132, 133 -- what I must be told before I sign`

@export As a buyer from the original subdivision owner, must I also be given the corporation's estimated budget and the owner's contracts and disclosures before I sign (Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) s 130(3), (4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the seller is the original subdivision owner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the seller is the developer who created the lot by the subdivision (the original subdivision owner)
      `the scheme is registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the community titles scheme has been registered
      `the first annual general meeting has been held` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the community corporation's first annual general meeting has been held
      `the seller's relative unit entitlement` IS A NUMBER @desc The fraction of the scheme's total unit entitlement carried by the lots the seller owns (for example 0.6)
      `a tier parcel carries half or more of the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a tier parcel in the scheme has a relative unit entitlement of 50% or more
      `the seller's share of that parcel's scheme` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, the fraction of the unit entitlement in that tier parcel's scheme carried by the seller's lots; otherwise 0
      `the seller otherwise controls half the voting power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the seller otherwise controls 50% or more of the voting power of the members
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`As a buyer must I be given the original subdivision owner's extra disclosures` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN `yes if` (`Must the seller give me its extra disclosures` `the seller is the original subdivision owner` `the scheme is registered` `the first annual general meeting has been held` `the seller's relative unit entitlement` `a tier parcel carries half or more of the scheme` `the seller's share of that parcel's scheme` `the seller otherwise controls half the voting power`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export As a buyer, may I postpone settlement because the seller has not given me the required information (Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) s 132)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the seller complied with s 130` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the seller gave the buyer everything s 130 requires before the contract was signed
      `the seller complied with s 131` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the seller notified every notifiable variation as s 131 requires (true if none occurred)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`As a buyer may I postpone settlement` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN `yes if` (`May I postpone settlement` `the seller complied with s 130` `the seller complied with s 131`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export As a buyer, may I avoid my contract because the seller did not give me the s 130 information before I signed (Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) s 133)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the seller complied with s 130` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the seller gave the buyer everything s 130 requires before the contract was signed
      `the missing information shows material prejudice to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the information not given would disclose material prejudice to you (you must prove it)
      `settlement has happened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract has already settled
      `the seller has since given substantially complying notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the seller has since given a notice substantially complying with s 130
      `working days since that notice` IS A NUMBER @desc Working days since that late notice was given (0 if none)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`As a buyer may I avoid my contract for missing disclosure` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN `yes if` (`May I avoid for missing disclosure` `the seller complied with s 130` `the missing information shows material prejudice to me` `settlement has happened` `the seller has since given substantially complying notice` `working days since that notice`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 3, 131, 134-136 -- a change between signing and settlement`

@export Did what changed between the signing of the contract and settlement amount to a type 1 or type 2 notifiable variation (Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) s 3(1); reg 8)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `something changed after the contract was signed and before settlement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether anything about the lot or the scheme changed after the contract of sale was signed and before settlement: its area, its unit entitlement, the scheme plan, by-laws, community development statement, services contracts, leases over common property, or termination papers served on the seller
      `the change` IS A `What changed before settlement` @desc What changed after the contract was signed and before settlement
GIVETH A `Notifiable variation, if it arises`
`What kind of notifiable variation is this change` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN
        IF `something changed after the contract was signed and before settlement`
        THEN `the variation kind, unless a sum is 0` `the change`
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    WHEN `I am selling a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN
        IF `something changed after the contract was signed and before settlement`
        THEN `the variation kind, unless a sum is 0` `the change`
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export As a buyer, may I avoid my contract because of a notifiable variation between signing and settlement (Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) ss 131, 134-136)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `something changed after the contract was signed and before settlement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether anything about the lot or the scheme changed after the contract of sale was signed and before settlement: its area, its unit entitlement, the scheme plan, by-laws, community development statement, services contracts, leases over common property, or termination papers served on the seller
      `the variation` IS A `Notifiable variation` @desc The kind of notifiable variation that occurred
      `the contract foretold it and it matched` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract described the proposed change and the change as completed matched (s 131(4))
      `the seller notified it in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the seller gave you notice of it within the time s 131(3) allows
      `the seller has given notice of it at all` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the seller has given you notice of the variation at any time
      `working days since the notice` IS A NUMBER @desc Working days since that notice was given (0 if none)
      `it materially prejudices me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are materially prejudiced by the variation (you must prove it)
      `settlement has happened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract has already settled
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`As a buyer may I avoid my contract for a notifiable variation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN
        IF `something changed after the contract was signed and before settlement`
        THEN `yes if` (`May I avoid for a notifiable variation` `the variation` `the contract foretold it and it matched` `the seller notified it in time` `the seller has given notice of it at all` `working days since the notice` `it materially prejudices me` `settlement has happened`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 137, 138 -- buying off the plan, and avoiding the contract`

@export As a buyer off the plan, may I avoid my contract because the deposit is not held on trust or my lot is not created in time (Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) s 137)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract is for a lot not yet created (off the plan)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract of sale was made before the lot was created by registration of the scheme or of an amendment of it (an off-the-plan contract)
      `the lot has been created` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the scheme (or the amendment creating your lot) has been registered, creating the lot
      `the contract has the deposit held on trust by a named practitioner or agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract requires the deposit to be held on trust for you by a lawyer, real estate agent or settlement agent it names
      `a period was agreed in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and the seller agreed in writing on a period for the lot to be created
      `the agreed period in months` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, that period in months; otherwise 0
      `whole months since the date of the contract` IS A NUMBER @desc Whole months since the contract was signed (by the last party to sign)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`As a buyer off the plan may I avoid my contract` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN
        IF `the contract is for a lot not yet created (off the plan)`
        THEN `yes if` (`May I avoid my off-the-plan contract` `the lot has been created` `the contract has the deposit held on trust by a named practitioner or agent` `a period was agreed in writing` `the agreed period in months` `whole months since the date of the contract`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export If I avoid my contract to buy a lot, how much do I get back, in dollars (Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) s 138(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract to buy the lot has been avoided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the buyer has avoided the contract of sale under Part 10 (by written notice to the seller stating the grounds, s 138(1))
      `the deposit held for me` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars held on your behalf as a deposit by an agent or practitioner
      `other money I paid the seller` IS A NUMBER @desc Any other dollars you paid the seller under the contract
      `rent due for my occupation` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars due to the seller as rent for any time you occupied the lot (0 if none)
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`As a buyer how much do I get back when I avoid` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN
        IF `the contract to buy the lot has been avoided`
        THEN amount (`How much do I get back` `the deposit held for me` `other money I paid the seller` `rent due for my occupation`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the seller of a lot`

§§§ `s 130 -- what I must give the buyer before they sign`

-- s 130(1): "Before a buyer signs a contract for the sale and purchase of a lot in a community titles scheme, the seller
-- of the lot must give the buyer" the seller's name and address, the scheme documents and the other information listed
-- in (b)-(e); (5): by a notice in the approved form, or in the contract; (6): the onus of proving it was given "lies on
-- the seller". Every seller, so the answer is yes for every seller.
@export Must I give the buyer the s 130 information and documents before they sign the contract (Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) s 130(1), (5), (6))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`As a seller must I give the buyer the s 130 information` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am selling a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN yes
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 130(3)-(4): the same five circumstances as the buyer's question, from the seller's side; the baseline's rule, with
-- "the seller is the original subdivision owner" asked as "I am".
@export As the seller, must I also give the buyer the corporation's estimated budget, my s 67 disclosures and the services contracts before they sign (Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) s 130(3), (4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am the original subdivision owner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the original subdivision owner (the developer) for the subdivision that created the lot
      `the scheme is registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the community titles scheme has been registered
      `the first annual general meeting has been held` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the community corporation's first annual general meeting has been held
      `the seller's relative unit entitlement` IS A NUMBER @desc The fraction of the scheme's total unit entitlement carried by the lots the seller owns (for example 0.6)
      `a tier parcel carries half or more of the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a tier parcel in the scheme has a relative unit entitlement of 50% or more
      `the seller's share of that parcel's scheme` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, the fraction of the unit entitlement in that tier parcel's scheme carried by the seller's lots; otherwise 0
      `the seller otherwise controls half the voting power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the seller otherwise controls 50% or more of the voting power of the members
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`As a seller must I give the extra s 130(4) disclosures` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am selling a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN `yes if` (`Must the seller give me its extra disclosures` `I am the original subdivision owner` `the scheme is registered` `the first annual general meeting has been held` `the seller's relative unit entitlement` `a tier parcel carries half or more of the scheme` `the seller's share of that parcel's scheme` `the seller otherwise controls half the voting power`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 3, 131 -- a change between signing and settlement`

-- The kind of variation is asked of the seller too, by the question "What kind of notifiable variation is this change"
-- above. Whether the change is a notifiable variation at all is the seller's to work out from it: this question takes
-- it as an input.
@export By when must I tell the buyer of a notifiable variation that occurred after they signed (Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) s 131(1), (3)-(5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `something changed after the contract was signed and before settlement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether anything about the lot or the scheme changed after the contract of sale was signed and before settlement: its area, its unit entitlement, the scheme plan, by-laws, community development statement, services contracts, leases over common property, or termination papers served on the seller
      `the variation` IS A `Notifiable variation` @desc The kind of notifiable variation that occurred
      `the contract described it and it was completed as described` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract told the buyer of the proposed action or matter, and it was completed as the contract described it (s 131(4)(a), (b))
      `working days before settlement when I became aware` IS A NUMBER @desc How many working days before the settlement date you became aware of the variation (or, if the contract described it, of its completion)
GIVETH A `When I must tell the buyer`
`By when must I tell the buyer of a notifiable variation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am selling a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN
        IF `something changed after the contract was signed and before settlement`
        THEN IF `the variation` EQUALS `no notifiable variation`
             THEN `does not arise for you`
             ELSE `the s 131 time for` `the contract described it and it was completed as described` `working days before settlement when I became aware`
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 137, 138 -- selling off the plan, and when the buyer avoids`

-- s 137(1)-(2): a contract "entered into before the lot is created" must "(a) require any deposit or other amount payable
-- by the buyer prior to registration ... to be paid by the buyer to a legal practitioner, real estate agent or
-- settlement agent to be held on trust for the buyer until the scheme is registered; and (b) specify the practitioner or
-- agent". Every off-the-plan contract, so yes where the situation holds.
@export Must my off-the-plan contract require the buyer's deposit to be paid to a named lawyer, real estate agent or settlement agent and held on trust (Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) s 137(1), (2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract is for a lot not yet created (off the plan)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract of sale was made before the lot was created by registration of the scheme or of an amendment of it (an off-the-plan contract)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must my off-the-plan contract have the deposit held on trust` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am selling a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN
        IF `the contract is for a lot not yet created (off the plan)`
        THEN yes
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 138(2)(a): "the buyer may recover from the seller as a debt all money paid by the buyer under the contract"; (b): the
-- holder of a deposit repays it, "minus any amount due to the seller as rent". Read as the baseline reads it (the buyer's
-- question): the holder repays the deposit less the rent, and the seller owes the rest of the money the buyer paid.
@export If the buyer avoids the contract, how much must I repay the buyer myself, in dollars (Community Titles Act 2018 (WA) s 138(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract to buy the lot has been avoided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the buyer has avoided the contract of sale under Part 10 (by written notice to the seller stating the grounds, s 138(1))
      `other money the buyer paid me` IS A NUMBER @desc The dollars the buyer paid you under the contract, other than a deposit held by an agent or practitioner
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`As a seller how much must I repay when the buyer avoids` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am selling a lot in a community titles scheme` THEN
        IF `the contract to buy the lot has been avoided`
        THEN amount (`How much do I get back` 0 `other money the buyer paid me` 0)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
